-- title:
--   Components of the resolved model have invertible ideal sheaves
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N_0 \neq 0$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel.html#L71) at level $\Gamma_0(N_0 q)$ (a structure packaging a proper, flat, integral, locally finitely presented model with normal affine sections, a curve model of the modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with its identification with the generic fibre, Galois equivariance of places, cusp expansions, smoothness and geometric integrality of the generic fibre, and the distinguished sections). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain equipped with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O$ from $R =$ [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.R q`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel.html#L32) whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $q$, and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$. Assume the site hypotheses $H$ of [`V3AsmLevel.SiteHyps`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSiteLevel.html#L270) (finiteness of the node set of the level site, existence of oriented crossing charts, an étale-neighbourhood datum, injectivity of the node-point assignment, closedness of each node point in the base change `DRLevel.XO`, and the model hypotheses on $q$ and $O$), and assume $h_\xi$: each of the points $\xi_j$ lies in the open subset `X0` of the chart input [`V3AsmLevel.C`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSiteLevel.html#L283), the complement of the finite set of distinguished node points. Then for every $v$ in the index type `X0MqComponents (width …)` the ideal sheaf datum [`V3AsmLevel.comp … v`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSiteLevel.html#L410) on the glued scheme $Y$ is invertible in the sense of `IsInvertible`: for every point $x$ of $Y$ there are an affine open $U$ and $f \in \Gamma(Y, U)$ with $x$ in the basic open $Y_f$, together with a non-zero-divisor $g$ of $\Gamma(Y, \text{affineBasicOpen } f)$ generating the ideal cut out by the datum on that affine basic open.
--
--   The components of the special fibre of the resolved (regular) model of $X_0(N_0 q)$ over $O$ are effective Cartier divisors, each being locally principal with non-zero-divisor generator. The result feeds into [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam), where the resolved model together with its charts is assembled.
